@startuml components
title M-UM1: component view within privileged process boundaries (unimplemented design)
left to right direction

actor "Configured caller\ninstaller / dispatcher UID" as Caller
component "sudo\ntrusted root transition; exact path, no args" as Sudo
package "swarma-user-manager process\nroot; one helper-op/1 invocation (v0)" {
  component "Sudo entry validation\neffective UID + SUDO_UID + argv" as MEntry
  component "Closed helper decoder\n16 KiB / 5 s" as MDecode
  component "Caller policy\nrole / ownership / quota" as MPolicy
  component "Lock, journal and recovery\ndependency recovery / bounded retire batches" as Recovery
  component "OS account backend\nmacOS dscl / Linux groupadd, useradd" as Accounts
  component "Descriptor-safe file operations\ntrusted directory descriptors; no-follow" as Files
  component "Retirement / metadata sweep\nquiescence; keys destroyed before deletion\nclosed-schema service-generated export only" as Archive
  component "Egress adapter\nv0 static range deny; v1 account narrowing\npf / nftables; evidence matrix" as Firewall
  component "Read-only effect.observe\noriginal caller / operator; six evidence states" as Observe
  component "Authorised exec.stop\nreceipt + live identity; TERM / KILL\naccount-wide absence ONLY; latest-receipt fence" as Stop
}
package "swarma-user-launcher process\nroot until privilege drop; one launch-op/1 invocation (v0)" {
  component "Sudo entry + closed decoder\n80 KiB / 5 s" as LEntry
  component "Launch validation\ncaller / generation / executor / home" as Launch
  component "Descriptor-safe executable / home opens\nno-follow; type / owner checks" as LFiles
  component "Receipt writer\natomic write before GID/UID drop" as Receipt
  component "R-FD3 descriptor lifecycle\nbounded immutable FD3; receipt/drop/exec ordering" as Exec
}
database "Root-owned configuration\nroles, ranges, metadata retention, approved digests\nInstaller places it (§11)" as Config
database "Root-owned manager control state\nledger + allocation cursor; lock; journal; audit\nlauncher-written start receipts; v1 applied state" as State
database "OS directory service\naccount / primary-group records\nmanager-created; backend storage" as OS
folder "Account-owned homes\nroot-controlled home roots\nRoot quarantine + metadata exports" as Homes
component "Kernel egress rules\nv0 range rule BEFORE accounts; v1 narrowing\nhelper-owned pf anchor / nftables table" as Kernel
component "curator-run -> harness\ntrusted agent UID; admitted executor path only" as Agent
component "swarma-credential-broker\nservice account; owns credentials / bindings / leases" as Broker
component "Read-only usage sampler (R-WATCH)\nleast OS-required privilege; root only if required\nno other authority; interface unpublished" as Sampler
component "Usage watcher\nper-class thresholds; interface unpublished" as Watcher
component "swarma-dispatcher\nworkspace contract / journaled stop owner" as Dispatcher
component "Approved workspace executors\nswarma-workspace-materialize / swarma-workspace-export\nchild UID; fixed environment; design labels" as Workspace
component "R-VERIFY runners\nisolated ephemeral; another machine; no secrets" as Verify
component "Session host\nservice UID; delivery / bound-board snapshots" as Host
component "Profile proxy (v1)\ntrusted service account; verified listener" as Proxy

actor "Operator phone\nsecure element; biometric gate" as Phone
actor "Operator terminal\npassword fallback; no cached ticket" as Terminal
component "operator command\nunder swarma-operator UID\nforced, narrow entry; no shell/harness" as Operator
component "swarma-observer\nmandatory protected service; read-only\nno shell/harness; no mutation/launcher" as Observer
Phone --> Operator : tailnet SSH; operator device key ONLY;\nsigned operator record over one act's canonical content
Terminal --> Operator : authenticated sudo; password;\nno NOPASSWD; timestamp_timeout=0
Operator --> Sudo : helper only; authenticated, non-cached rule
Observer --> State : public ledger accounts read; no confirmation
Caller --> Sudo : operation JSON on stdin
Sudo --> MEntry
Sudo --> LEntry : configured dispatcher ONLY
MEntry --> MDecode
MDecode --> MPolicy
MPolicy --> Config
MPolicy --> Recovery
Recovery --> State : shared transition lock; journal before actions; bounded batches yield
Recovery --> Accounts
Recovery --> Archive
Recovery --> Firewall
Recovery --> Stop
Recovery --> Observe
Observe --> State : journal-serialized evidence; no new mutation
Accounts --> OS
Accounts --> Files
Archive --> Files
Files --> Homes
Firewall --> Kernel
Firewall --> Proxy : verify owner/generation AND served digest; no shared lock across query
Firewall --> State : publish applied state after successful apply
Stop --> State : matching root start receipt
Stop --> Agent : latest receipt/current generation; TERM/KILL same UID set; quiet absence
LEntry --> Launch
Launch --> Config
Launch --> State : same transition lock + bounded dependency recovery; active owned generation
Launch --> LFiles : no-follow executable / home
LFiles --> Homes : opened home as cwd
Launch --> Receipt
Receipt --> State
Receipt --> Exec
Exec --> Agent : admitted harness executor only; standard FDs + FD3 plan
Exec --> Workspace : approved child-UID exec; materialize before work;\nexport only after confirmed absence
Dispatcher --> Workspace : immutable admitted plans via launcher; no repository held
Workspace --> Homes : private standalone repository; export data before retirement
Workspace --> Dispatcher : bounded change set; no worker Git history
Sampler --> State : read-only generation attribution
Sampler --> Homes : read-only home usage
Sampler --> Kernel : read-only network / refused counters
Sampler --> Agent : read-only CPU / memory / process count
Sampler --> Watcher : per-UID telemetry
Watcher --> Dispatcher : hard threshold: one-account freeze + journaled exec.stop
Watcher --> Phone : operator alerts; unpublished format
Operator --> Dispatcher : R-ALLSTOP: authentication + one confirmation; hold admission
Operator --> Firewall : authorized range flip to deny-all; journaled
Dispatcher --> Stop : every agent / workplace generation; confirmed absence
Operator --> Broker : freeze leases / renewals; delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime
Operator --> Host : close delivery; snapshot bound boards
Dispatcher --> Verify : board-owned controlled verification; results as data
Agent --> Broker : trusted agent only; fresh connection / lease
Broker --> State : reads ledger / v1 applied state; readability is not authority

note bottom of Recovery
  Refusal: invalid invocation/schema, role, ownership, quota, unmanaged objects,
  request_id conflict, unsafe path (§§2-6). Terminal same effect replays recorded
  result plus current state; admitted stop/retire pending continues same effect.
  Recovery validates shared integrity/accounting, then dependencies, not all retirements.
  Bounded cleanup batches yield lock; reservations/fences remain until full cleanup.
  R-LOCK: no synchronous platform-service call under state lock; per-record in-flight marker.
end note
note bottom of Launch
  Refusal: inactive/wrong-owner generation, unapproved executor, digest mismatch,
  existing execution receipt, failed privilege drop (§7).
  Resolve ambiguous launch through same effect/receipt; never a second start (§§4.6, 7).
  Retain generation lock through receipt and verified UID/GID drop; executable handle through exec.
  Scrub untrusted inherited FDs first; close internal handles at last use / qualified close-on-exec;
  release on every failure. Executor receives only 0-2 and read-only immutable FD3 (R-FD3).
  Dispatcher alone invokes launcher; host requests host_start from dispatcher.
  I4 joint admission/permit/fence publication remains gated (§14 question 3).
end note
note bottom of Stop
  TERM/KILL and verification cover every current-generation UID process, including escaped/OS starts.
  Latest receipt fence on every continuation; terminal stop replay never signals.
  No harness native-lock attestation (§4.7).
  Session-host recovery: fresh agent-UID runner checks native lock under closed fence;
  unknown result keeps parked (session-host §3.5).
end note
note bottom of Archive
  Destroy declared keys before home deletion; failure/unknown keeps retiring (§4.4.1).
  Delete all home content/names/links through descriptors; no classification.
  R-TRANSFER workspace export recorded BEFORE retirement, or explicit operator waiver.
  Retirement export only closed-schema service-generated metadata; no agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies.
  Export schema/provenance/naming/bounds and audit encoding open (§14 question 6).
  Separate swarma-operator retention: authentication + exact-content confirmation;
  refused inside agent sessions; confidentiality not guaranteed; format unpublished (§14 questions 1, 17).
end note
note bottom of Observe
  recorded + current state; pending; rolled_back; not_recorded; unavailable; contradictory (R-OBS).
  Only complete authoritative evidence proves not_recorded; expiry/read failure -> unavailable.
  Original principal may observe after mutation-grant expiry; no new effect is authorised.
  Evidence retained until permanent inadmissibility; exact bounds/coverage open (§14 question 8).
end note
note bottom of Firewall
  R-NETBIND: root-owned binding beside user-manager.json; dispatcher pins at prepare.
  Verify served digest; re-apply existing allocations flushes kernel/old proxy sessions.
  R-SVC-EGRESS: dispatcher/host deny-all, broker via own proxy; resolver sandbox qualified.
  Installer owns start-time and periodic service-policy checks; lapse drops readiness.
  R-RANGE-DENY: range 30000-59999 before accounts; v0 proxy listeners only.
  Install/start/scheduled test-UID precedence probe: any earlier quick match -> incident/readiness drop.
  R-NET-TOOL: workplaces ZERO egress, no loopback/proxy exception.
  Linux network namespace + Unix-only families; macOS deny-network sandbox + per-UID deny.
  R-SOCKETS: test UID reaches exactly declared platform sockets, no other sockets.
  R-WORKPLACE: helper v1 enforced activation; rb-exec under service UID.
  v1: refuse unsupported tuple; never report enforcement without whole-matrix evidence.
  Denial before first launch; retain until account/group removal (§8).
end note
note "Defining spec: [[../spec/helper.md#1-purpose §1 process split]], [[../spec/helper.md#2-invocation §§2-3 invocation/policy]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#46-lock-journal-and-idempotency §4.6 recovery]], [[../spec/helper.md#6-file-operations §6 paths]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher §7 launcher]], [[../spec/helper.md#8-firewall-per-account-v1 §8 egress]].\nBoxes are conceptual responsibilities within binaries, not implemented classes or extra processes.\nCurrent: nothing implemented; v0 accounts/launcher/static range rule, v1 narrowing, v2 grants (§13).\nv0/v1 refuse grants; v2 subject-bound chain checks target/time/revocation (§9); signature grammar open.\nSH2+ joint admission remains gated by I4 publication (§§7, 14); dispatcher alone invokes the launcher.\nDonor provisioning is a separate component; variant B disabled pending its spec (§1.1)." as Scope
Scope .. MEntry
note bottom of State
  R-GEN: fresh random 128-bit generations, ledger store epoch and reader floors.
  External restore mark closes every consumer before restored bytes; surviving evidence reconciled.
  No retirement resurrection; lost coverage unavailable, never not_recorded (§4.6.1).
  R-FATE process table at §7: selected kill domains / affected sets qualify before activation.
  Every supervisor write checks durable daemon-instance epoch; no live adoption.
end note
note bottom of Operator
  swarma-operator: protected service; helper operator UID, broker operator/account owner,
  holder of broker v0 root and operator signing authority; never a harness account.
  Machine verifies act-bound signature against pinned phone key; no reuse for another act.
  App shows who/actions/until; widening requires authentication + exact-content confirmation;
  CLI refuses all operator acts inside agent sessions. Revocation: one biometric confirmation.
  Command binary/wire, signature domain/canonical bytes, exact sshd config,
  OS entry and phone-to-helper authenticated transition unpublished (§14 question 17).
  No signature-algorithm change mandated; root/device compatibility remains publication work.
end note
note bottom of Observer
  Reads: status, grants, accounts, bindings without confirmation; interfaces unpublished.
  No other principal's private effect.observe journal access (§§2-3, 14 question 17).
  Installer or operator creates both protected service-class accounts; dispatcher cannot (§4.3).
  NOPASSWD stays only for dispatcher helper/launcher rules; operator/installer authenticate.
end note
note bottom of Workspace
  R-TRANSFER: exact B + manifest digest + write scope + exec profile covered by plan digest.
  No hooks/remotes/credential helpers; no linked cross-account worktrees.
  Whole-export refusals and caps; only original requester gets digested result.
  Board accepts resource only; orchestrator imports signed C, exact-commit independent review,
  rework from C and signed fast-forward through existing board path (§7).
  Formats/caps/interlocks unpublished (§14 question 15); no general launcher copy operation.
end note
note bottom of Sampler
  CPU, memory, process count, home disk, network and refused connections incl. mail ports.
  Watcher never kills without journal; node-wide stop manual only (§§8.2-8.3).
  Partial/unknown R-ALLSTOP is incident; admission closed; explicit recovery, no restart.
end note
note bottom of Agent
  R-EXEC: OS exec allowlist; writable areas non-executable; protected shared-tool wrapper only.
  No account-started harness/agent environment, builds/tests/downloads or heavy tools.
  R-CEILINGS: selected root-created non-delegated Linux unit; qualified macOS mechanisms.
  R-STANDING: trusted local loop only; plan surfaces verified before launch/restart/native resume.
  Untrusted standing workplace loop stays at donor; no subscription binding/lease.
  R-SHARED: no shared services beside untrusted work; publish host capability matrix.
end note
@enduml
